 "pages": "p.3 (DGS pins), p.4 (YCJ balls), p.5 (ROC: VDD 2-3.6 V, digital inputs GND-3.6 V), p.12 (data rates 128-3300 SPS, 1/DR), p.14 (conversion-ready setup, 8 us pulse), p.15 (power-up in single-shot power-down), p.16 (ADDR GND/VDD/SDA/SCL -> 48h/49h/4Ah/4Bh), p.17 (25 ms timeout, general call 06h), p.18 (pointer write then read), p.19 (format), p.20-23 (registers)",
 "notModeled": [
  "analog inputs, PGA and internal reference (PGA is stored only); the result is the 0 V code",
  "OS=1 writes during a running conversion or in continuous mode: the datasheet says no effect (the engine may restart)",
  "continuous mode: a configuration write lets the running conversion finish with the old settings",
  "~25 us power-up before a single-shot conversion (folded into the conversion time: not added)",
  "conversion time 1 / nominal data rate; the internal oscillator drift is not modeled",
  "a floating ADDR pin (not specified); the SDA strap needs SDA held low 100 ns after SCL falls",
  "I2C timeout (bus idle 25 ms mid-transaction resets the interface); standard/fast mode only (no Fm+/Hs); VIH 1 V for 1.8-V buses; I2C timing limits",
  "comparator: traditional/window modes, COMP_POL polarity, COMP_LAT latching, COMP_QUE assert count, SMBus alert response (ALERT/RDY works only as the conversion-ready pin; COMP_POL and the rest are stored only)",
  "multiplexer: MUX selects 4 differential / 4 single-ended pairs (stored; [CH] is the MUX code 0-7)"
 ],
 "variants": "ADS1014L / ADS1015L share ads1014l.pdf (ADS1014L: AIN2/AIN3 are NC and MUX reserved); own spec files. Register-compatible with ADS1014/ADS1015 at VDD 2-3.6 V",
